            "id": "fr-p18-explain-form",
            "type": "explain",
            "heading": "Indefinite articles",
            "explanation": "The source distinguishes un for a masculine singular noun, une for a feminine singular noun and des for plural. Livre is masculine, table feminine. Learn the noun with its gender; spelling alone does not always identify it.",
            "conceptIds": []
          },
          {
            "id": "fr-p18-explain-context",
            "type": "explain",
            "heading": "Definite reference and elision",
            "explanation": "The source distinguishes le, la, l’ and les for definite reference. Before a vowel or mute h, singular le/la elides to l’, as in L’école est ouverte. L’ does not reveal the noun's gender. Le livre est sur la table contrasts masculine le with feminine la.",
            "conceptIds": []
          },
          {
            "id": "fr-p18-guided",
            "type": "guided",
            "exerciseIds": [
              "fr-p18-gender",
